# netsurf: rounded corners drawn (patch 363, with 363-libcss)
# Generated 2026-11-01
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 361)
#
# The Vita never drew border-radius: plot_style.border_radius was set and
# no plotter read it, so every box was square (doc 11 recorded it as the
# Vita's limitation). Pills, cards, avatars' backgrounds and rounded
# buttons now draw rounded, through the antialiased path filler (359).
#
#  - redraw_border.c: html_redraw_corner_radii() resolves the four corners
#    to device px (percentages of the border box) and shrinks overlapping
#    radii together (CSS backgrounds 5.5); html_redraw_rounded_shape()
#    emits a rounded rectangle -- or a ring, the inner one wound the
#    other way -- as a flattened path (<= 16 segments a corner) through
#    ctx->plot->path; html_redraw_borders_rounded() draws a border whose
#    drawn sides are all solid and one colour as one ring, with the
#    colour's alpha and the group opacity folded as the square painter
#    does (html_redraw_border_can_round() is the test).
#  - redraw.c: a box's own solid background colour (not the canvas
#    propagated from root/body, no macsurf transform, background-clip
#    border-box) with any corner radius fills the rounded shape; a box
#    whose border cannot be rounded keeps a square background too, so a
#    square border never shows corner wedges. The ring is tried before
#    html_redraw_borders().
#  - getComputedStyle answers the four corners (borderTopLeftRadius ...,
#    "H" or "H V") and borderRadius as their shorthand; CSS.supports
#    knows the corner and logical names (vita_polyfill.js / .inc).
#
# Still square: background images and gradients, inline boxes'
# backgrounds, box-shadow, overflow clipping of children (an <img> with
# border-radius: 50% stays a square photo), and borders of mixed colour
# or style. Device cost: one path per rounded box, the 359 frame-pool
# budget falls back to centre-sampled fills; not yet measured on the Vita.
#
